usage: run.py [-h] --baseline BASELINE [--candidate CANDIDATE]
              [--qualification QUALIFICATION] [--upstream UPSTREAM] --work
              WORK [--evidence EVIDENCE]
              {g0,serial,parallel,smoke,negative-validation}

Temporary #1250 G0–G2 orchestration; existing pytest nodes remain the oracle.
Run as PID 1 in a disposable Linux PID/mount namespace. Only direct
subprocesses are waited for: adopted zombies deliberately remain observable
until namespace exit. Subjects are separate frozen checkouts; mutations occur
only in scratch clones. Any unexpected exit, count, skip, drift or failure
aborts advancement. The controller consumes a read-only job token over stdin
before subject execution. No full environment dumps, G3–G5 or dispatch
operations. Same-UID/root access is outside the accepted boundary; this is not
a credential secrecy sandbox.

positional arguments:
  {g0,serial,parallel,smoke,negative-validation}

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --baseline BASELINE
  --candidate CANDIDATE
  --qualification QUALIFICATION
  --upstream UPSTREAM
  --work WORK
  --evidence EVIDENCE
